                    {
                        "form_id": "984f58d1-0d0a-4ab5-bdfd-dbcd4467587f",
                        "entry_id": "4b0f469a-7ff7-398c-a034-96091522264a",
                        "tags": [
                            "accusative",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "die Universalien"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7c06eb04-95ae-3341-821a-e46539ad3dd2",
                        "entry_id": "4b0f469a-7ff7-398c-a034-96091522264a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Eigenschaft, die allen Sprachen gemeinsam ist"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b093d1d-c5fe-4503-b9cd-e99ef542ca5d",
                                "sense_id": "7c06eb04-95ae-3341-821a-e46539ad3dd2",
                                "text": "Die Linguistik, speziell die Universalienforschung, erforscht die Eigenschaften, die alle Sprachen miteinander teilen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce21be20-1f22-433b-80d3-f5314d975b4c",
                                "sense_id": "7c06eb04-95ae-3341-821a-e46539ad3dd2",
                                "text": "„Ein breites Vergleichsfixum liefern die von H. Haarmann auf der Grundlage von 65 europäischen Sprachen gewonnenen »europäischen Universalien« (›Europeme‹).“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9af84625-c5df-464f-87c3-0bc0dc258ff1",
                                "sense_id": "7c06eb04-95ae-3341-821a-e46539ad3dd2",
                                "text": "„Nach dieser vorgängigen Warnung versucht er, einige allgemeine Tendenzen semantischen Wandels zu zeigen, in denen er mögliche Kandidaten für Universalien sieht.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ccbc653-9c2a-49d7-99be-2f58d53ea782",
                                "sense_id": "7c06eb04-95ae-3341-821a-e46539ad3dd2",
                                "text": "„Dieses kindliche Vermögen sei in den linguistischen Universalien manifestiert.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c5856947-d0a0-38b9-b92c-98c086ff94bb",
                        "entry_id": "4b0f469a-7ff7-398c-a034-96091522264a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "allgemeiner Art- oder Gattungsbegriff, über dessen Status im Mittelalter (9. bis 13. Jahrhundert) gestritten wurde"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d544c1fe-6dd5-48f5-a784-41f411581359",
                                "sense_id": "c5856947-d0a0-38b9-b92c-98c086ff94bb",
                                "text": "Besonders in der mittelalterlichen Philosophie der Scholastik spielen Universalien eine große Rolle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16fefb1c-8865-40e0-bed4-14e2c832dafe",
                                "sense_id": "c5856947-d0a0-38b9-b92c-98c086ff94bb",
                                "text": "„Die Auffassung über die Universalien änderte sich dann im Verlaufe der scholastischen Philosophie und […] so teilt man die Scholastik […] in drei Perioden ein.“ Die platonisch geprägte Frühscholastik („Universalia sunt ante res.“), die aristotelisch geprägte Hochscholastik („Universalia sunt in rebus.“) und die nominalistisch geprägte Spätscholastik („Universalia sunt post res.“)."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c58c6c1a-d7d4-4fc3-95a7-cc7851dd3390",
                        "source_entry_id": "4b0f469a-7ff7-398c-a034-96091522264a",
                        "source_sense_id": "7c06eb04-95ae-3341-821a-e46539ad3dd2",
                        "source_sense_description": "Linguistik: Eigenschaft, die allen Sprachen gemeinsam ist",
                        "target_lang_word": "universal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "universal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2f2e3824-4197-3587-a849-28d1cf298610",
                                        "entry_id": "c50214fd-8b79-316a-9388-04f99ea39646",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to the universe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f138ef28-559d-3883-ac6d-c9eeeb3ebf9f",
                                        "entry_id": "c50214fd-8b79-316a-9388-04f99ea39646",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Common to all members of a group or class."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93846a36-4fd4-403b-b4df-544ac3d6697c",
                                                "sense_id": "f138ef28-559d-3883-ac6d-c9eeeb3ebf9f",
                                                "text": "In Logic, the letter A is used as a symbol for the universal affirmative proposition in the general form \"all x is y.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1150bf0e-e059-4979-adef-0d67e9dddd01",
                                                "sense_id": "f138ef28-559d-3883-ac6d-c9eeeb3ebf9f",
                                                "text": "I had been planning every day through these years toward a universal car."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9dc0a09-d15b-4071-a7fd-2dca06ba0f51",
                                                "sense_id": "f138ef28-559d-3883-ac6d-c9eeeb3ebf9f",
                                                "text": "Eventually, the railway opened on Monday, December 14, 1896, with a universal fare of 1d. collected at the turnstiles, and conditions were immediately chaotic, as many passengers travelled round and round, and refused to leave the cars."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f956786-1144-4fba-ac59-b627984ae4c6",
                                                "sense_id": "f138ef28-559d-3883-ac6d-c9eeeb3ebf9f",
                                                "text": "Sutton SignWriting is the universal and complete solution for written sign language, ISO 15924 script code \"Sgnw\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f9a4b6a-f65a-3c55-9579-fb251cda7355",
                                        "entry_id": "c50214fd-8b79-316a-9388-04f99ea39646",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Common to all society; worldwide."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "829b9a3a-cda8-421b-a677-7c63e15a2108",
                                                "sense_id": "7f9a4b6a-f65a-3c55-9579-fb251cda7355",
                                                "text": "She achieved universal fame."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6cd858f1-4d01-45b7-93b3-3ae1f5d936e3",
                                                "sense_id": "7f9a4b6a-f65a-3c55-9579-fb251cda7355",
                                                "text": "[John] Dryden's univerſal genius, his firmly eſtablished reputation, and the glory his memory muſt always reflect upon the nation that gave him birth, make us ardently wiſh for a more accurate life of him than any which has hitherto appeared: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7ca7f5a6-0c33-333e-952c-3e3e3fcbe064",
                                        "entry_id": "c50214fd-8b79-316a-9388-04f99ea39646",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unlimited; vast; infinite."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45a20740-6367-38c2-a716-4d33a708dee5",
                                        "entry_id": "c50214fd-8b79-316a-9388-04f99ea39646",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Useful for many purposes; all-purpose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c524f3c-2a2e-4d9a-9457-7913b6982370",
                                                "sense_id": "45a20740-6367-38c2-a716-4d33a708dee5",
                                                "text": "universal wrench"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "universal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "490d4935-0a78-3efd-bf75-fcf484ace1b9",
                                        "entry_id": "cf1d6d9b-dc95-3b6f-8b11-b38dc6995f82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A characteristic or property that particular things have in common."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "deaafd37-667f-4fc8-8d53-93f8caafc1e4",
                                                "sense_id": "490d4935-0a78-3efd-bf75-fcf484ace1b9",
                                                "text": "When we examine common words, we find that, broadly speaking, proper names stand for particulars, while other substantives, adjectives, prepositions, and verbs stand for universals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f16c612-c15e-4038-8a18-1f06a3fb82b9",
                                                "sense_id": "490d4935-0a78-3efd-bf75-fcf484ace1b9",
                                                "text": "We might also distinguish those expressions which are used to refer to individuals or particulars from those which are used to refer to what philosophers have called universals: e.g., to distinguish such expressions as \"Everest\" and \"this chair\" from \"the number three\", \"the color red\" and \"drunkenness\"."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cefaab8c-8b55-454a-b630-4443a8019dd0",
                                                "sense_id": "490d4935-0a78-3efd-bf75-fcf484ace1b9",
                                                "text": "Empiricism was similarly a response to this loss of universals—a radically contingent world with no underlying order must constantly be studied and tested—and made God himself unnecessary: divine spirit and human spirit were alien enough to each other that they could function without taking each other into account."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
